          "sha": "99380529b9e688e5fd41df3f5364518f3cde4759",
          "message": "ci: add continuous BenchmarkDotNet publishing workflow (#791)\n\n* ci: add continuous BenchmarkDotNet publishing workflow\n\nAdds a new GitHub Actions workflow that runs the benchmarks in\ntest/OpenFeature.Benchmarks on push to main, daily on a schedule, and\nvia manual dispatch. Results are published to the gh-pages branch\nusing martincostello/benchmarkdotnet-results-publisher for tracking\nperformance over time via a GitHub Pages dashboard.\n\nAlso adds net8.0 to the benchmarks project's target frameworks so the\nexisting SimpleJob(RuntimeMoniker.Net80, baseline: true) benchmark job\ncan build and run in CI.\n\nCloses #625\n\nSigned-off-by: Berk Selvi <berkslv@gmail.com>\n\n* Potential fix for pull request finding\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot Autofix powered by AI <175728472+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nSigned-off-by: Berk Selvi <54676516+berkslv@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* ci: harden benchmark workflow permissions and add concurrency control\n\n- Set persist-credentials: false on checkout since only the publisher\n  step needs write access, and it authenticates via its own repo-token\n  input rather than relying on ambient git credentials.\n- Add a concurrency group so overlapping push/schedule/dispatch runs\n  cannot race when pushing results to gh-pages.\n- Scope 'dotnet restore' to the benchmarks project explicitly instead\n  of restoring the whole repository.\n\nAddresses review feedback from CodeRabbit and Copilot on PR #791.\n\nSigned-off-by: Berk Selvi <berkslv@gmail.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Berk Selvi <berkslv@gmail.com>\nSigned-off-by: Berk Selvi <54676516+berkslv@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Copilot Autofix powered by AI <175728472+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>",
